(vector (map (:db/id -1)
 (:adr/id "adr-2607231835-atlas-mercury-reverse-domain-isic-ownership")
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/source-format "edn")
  (:adr/title "Atlas/Mercury integration ownership — reverse-domain adapters, ISIC workflows, ISCO metadata")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-07-23")
  (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-23")
  (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki"))
  (:adr/authoritative true)
  (:adr/topic "atlas-mercury-repository-ownership")
  (:adr/repos (vector "orgs/kotoba-lang/com-stripe"
              "orgs/kotoba-lang/com-mercury"
              "orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6910"
              "orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6419"))
  (:adr/related (vector "adr-2606302300-org-taxonomy-4-orgs"
                "adr-2607041500"))
  (:adr/supersedes (vector))
  (:adr/superseded_by (vector))
  (:adr/authoritative_for
  (vector "ownership of Stripe Atlas and Mercury provider-specific contracts"
   "separation of reverse-domain provider adapters from ISIC business workflows"
   "use of ISCO codes as role metadata rather than product or provider repo identity"))
  (:adr/problem
  (map (:gap "A cross-provider atlas-mercury-onboarding repository mixed company formation, banking operations, Stripe contracts, and Mercury contracts.")
   (:risk "Provider names bypass reverse-domain naming, business workflows duplicate existing ISIC repositories, and ISCO may be incorrectly treated as a product classification.")))
  (:adr/decision
  (map (:provider-contracts
   (map ("stripe.com" "kotoba-lang/com-stripe")
    ("mercury.com" "kotoba-lang/com-mercury")))
   (:business-workflows
   (map ("ISIC-6910" "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6910")
    ("ISIC-6419" "cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6419")))
   (:occupation-metadata
   (map ("ISCO-1346" "financial and insurance services branch managers")
    ("ISCO-3312" "credit and loans officers")
    ("ISCO-2611" "lawyers, where legal work is actually performed")))
   (:cross-provider-composition
   "Document handoffs at the owning provider boundary; do not create a compound vendor-name repository.")
   (:duplicate-repository
   (map (:repo "cloud-itonami/atlas-mercury-onboarding")
    (:disposition :archived)
    (:deleted false)))))
  (:adr/consequences
  (vector "Stripe Atlas contracts and payment-account cutover guidance live in com-stripe."
   "Mercury-specific contracts and security boundaries live in com-mercury."
   "Company-formation process and provider profile live in ISIC 6910."
   "Monetary-intermediation intake and activation controls live in ISIC 6419."
   "ISCO codes describe participating human occupations only; they do not name Atlas, Mercury, or their repositories."
   "The duplicate cross-domain repository remains archived for recoverable history and points to maintained locations."))
  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607231835: Atlas/Mercury integration ownership\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-23\n**Decider**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Context\n\nA temporary `cloud-itonami/atlas-mercury-onboarding` repository and a\n`kotoba-lang/stripe-mercury-integration` repository were created while\npreparing a Stripe Atlas company for Mercury onboarding. The first crossed two\nindustry activities and two providers; the second did not follow\n`kotoba-lang/com-*` reverse-domain naming.\n\nISIC classifies economic activity. ISCO classifies occupations. Neither is a\nsubstitute for the provider boundary represented by a reverse-domain adapter.\nExisting repositories already own the relevant activities: ISIC 6910 for legal\nand company-formation work, and ISIC 6419 for monetary intermediation.\n\n## Decision\n\nProvider-specific contracts use reverse-domain repositories:\n\n- Stripe and Stripe Atlas: `kotoba-lang/com-stripe`\n- Mercury: `kotoba-lang/com-mercury`\n\nBusiness workflows remain in their ISIC repositories:\n\n- formation and incorporation handoff: `cloud-itonami-isic-6910`\n- account intake and banking activation controls: `cloud-itonami-isic-6419`\n\nISCO 1346, 3312, and—when legal work is genuinely involved—2611 may be\nrecorded as participating-role metadata. ISCO never names a provider or product\nrepository.\n\nCross-provider orchestration is expressed as handoff documentation between the\nowning repositories. A compound repository named after multiple vendors is not\ncreated.\n\n## Execution record\n\nOn 2026-07-23:\n\n1. `kotoba-lang/stripe-mercury-integration` was renamed to\n   `kotoba-lang/com-mercury`.\n2. Atlas handoff guidance was added to `kotoba-lang/com-stripe`.\n3. The Atlas formation profile was added to `cloud-itonami-isic-6910`.\n4. The Mercury provider profile was added to `cloud-itonami-isic-6419`.\n5. `cloud-itonami/atlas-mercury-onboarding` was marked archived, not deleted,\n   with maintained-location pointers.\n\n## Consequences\n\nEvery fact has one owner: provider API semantics in `com-*`, industry workflow\nin `cloud-itonami-isic-*`, and human occupation codes as metadata. Historical\nwork remains recoverable without inviting further edits in the obsolete\ncross-domain repository.")))
